  "recipe-section-1": {
    "markdown": "- **Russet potatoes:** 500 g (cooked and peeled)\n- **Egg yolks:** 2 large egg yolks\n- **Whole milk:** 118 mL\n- **Shredded cheese:** 500 g total (divided into two 250 g portions)\n- **Potato Seasonings:** 19.5 mL sea salt (added in two 10 mL steps) , 29.5 mL black pepper, 15 mL dill, 29.5 mL garlic powder (divided) , 15 mL oregano , 15 mL rosemary, 5 mL lemon pepper , and 10 mL beef bouillon powder. Extra dill for garnishing the top",
    "html": "<ul class=\"ingredient-list\">\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Russet potatoes: 500 g (cooked and peeled)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-1\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Russet potatoes:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"500 g\" data-original=\"500g\" data-us=\"17.64 oz\" title=\"Source: 500g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">500 g</span> (cooked and peeled) </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Egg yolks: 2 large egg yolks\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-2\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Egg yolks:</strong> 2 large egg yolks </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Whole milk: 118 mL\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-3\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Whole milk:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"118 mL\" data-original=\"1/2 cup\" data-us=\"½ cup\" title=\"Source: 1/2 cup. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">118 mL</span> </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Shredded cheese: 500 g total (divided into two 250 g portions)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-4\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Shredded cheese:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"500 g\" data-original=\"500g\" data-us=\"17.64 oz\" title=\"Source: 500g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">500 g</span> total (divided into two <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"250 g\" data-original=\"250g\" data-us=\"8.82 oz\" title=\"Source: 250g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">250 g</span> portions) </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Potato Seasonings: 19.5 mL sea salt (added in two 10 mL steps) , 29.5 mL black pepper, 15 mL dill, 29.5 mL garlic powder (divided) , 15 mL oregano , 15 mL rosemary, 5 mL lemon pepper , and 10 mL beef bouillon powder. Extra dill for garnishing the top\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-5\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Potato Seasonings:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"19.5 mL\" data-original=\"4 tsps\" data-us=\"4 tsp\" title=\"Source: 4 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">19.5 mL</span> sea salt (added in two <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2-tsp\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2-tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> steps) , <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> black pepper, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 mL\" data-original=\"1 tbsp\" data-us=\"1 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tbsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">15 mL</span> dill, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> garlic powder (divided) , <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 mL\" data-original=\"1 tbsp\" data-us=\"1 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tbsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">15 mL</span> oregano , <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 mL\" data-original=\"1 tbsp\" data-us=\"1 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tbsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">15 mL</span> rosemary, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"5 mL\" data-original=\"1 tsp\" data-us=\"1 tsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">5 mL</span> lemon pepper , and <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> beef bouillon powder. Extra dill for garnishing the top</div></li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-1",
    "title": "For the Cheesy Potato Layer",
    "heading_html": "For the Cheesy Potato Layer"
  },
  "recipe-section-2": {
    "markdown": "- **Ground beef:** 1 kg\n- **Olive oil:** 29.5 mL\n- **Large white onion:** 1 onion (processed finely)\n- **Garlic cloves:** 8 to 9 cloves (pressed)\n- **Vodka:** 100 mL (a heavy splash)\n- **Water:** 237 mL\n- **All-purpose flour:** 30 g (approx. 15 g to thicken the gravy)\n- **Tomato paste:** 59–74 mL\n- **Frozen mixed vegetables:** 237 mL (peas and carrots work best)\n- **Meat Seasonings:** 29.5 mL chicken bouillon powder, 29.5 mL lemon pepper, 29.5 mL Tajín, 5 mL ginger powder, 29.5 mL garlic powder, 10 mL rosemary, 10 mL oregano, 10 mL dill, and 5 mL sea salt",
    "html": "<ul class=\"ingredient-list\">\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Ground beef: 1 kg\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-6\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Ground beef:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"1 kg\" data-original=\"1000g\" data-us=\"2.2 lb\" title=\"Source: 1000g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">1 kg</span></div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Olive oil: 29.5 mL\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-7\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Olive oil:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span></div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Large white onion: 1 onion (processed finely)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-8\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Large white onion:</strong> 1 onion (processed finely)</div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Garlic cloves: 8 to 9 cloves (pressed)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-9\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Garlic cloves:</strong> 8 to 9 cloves (pressed)</div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Vodka: 100 mL (a heavy splash)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-10\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Vodka:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"100 mL\" data-original=\"100ml\" data-us=\"0.42 cup\" title=\"Source: 100ml. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">100 mL</span> (a heavy splash)</div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Water: 237 mL\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-11\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Water:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"237 mL\" data-original=\"1 cup\" data-us=\"1 cup\" title=\"Source: 1 cup. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">237 mL</span> </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off All-purpose flour: 30 g (approx. 15 g to thicken the gravy)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-12\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>All-purpose flour:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"30 g\" data-original=\"30g\" data-us=\"¼ cup\" title=\"Source: 30g. flour: 120 g per US cup (ingredient-specific estimate)\">30 g</span> (approx. <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 g\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. flour: 120 g per US cup (ingredient-specific estimate)\">15 g</span> to thicken the gravy) </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Tomato paste: 59–74 mL\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-13\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Tomato paste:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"59–74 mL\" data-original=\"4 to 5 tbsps\" data-us=\"4–5 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 4 to 5 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">59–74 mL</span> </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Frozen mixed vegetables: 237 mL (peas and carrots work best)\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-14\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Frozen mixed vegetables:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"237 mL\" data-original=\"1 full cup\" data-us=\"1 cup\" title=\"Source: 1 full cup. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">237 mL</span> (peas and carrots work best) </div></li>\n<li class=\"ingredient-item\"><input aria-label=\"Check off Meat Seasonings: 29.5 mL chicken bouillon powder, 29.5 mL lemon pepper, 29.5 mL Tajín, 5 mL ginger powder, 29.5 mL garlic powder, 10 mL rosemary, 10 mL oregano, 10 mL dill, and 5 mL sea salt\" class=\"ingredient-checkbox\" id=\"ing-instant-pot-cottage-pie-15\" type=\"checkbox\"/><div class=\"ingredient-copy\"><strong>Meat Seasonings:</strong> <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> chicken bouillon powder, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> lemon pepper, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> Tajín, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"5 mL\" data-original=\"1 tsp\" data-us=\"1 tsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">5 mL</span> ginger powder, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> garlic powder, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> rosemary, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> oregano, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> dill, and <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"5 mL\" data-original=\"1 tsp\" data-us=\"1 tsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">5 mL</span> sea salt</div></li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-2",
    "title": "For the Beef Matrix",
    "heading_html": "For the Beef Matrix"
  },
  "recipe-section-4": {
    "markdown": "- Preheat your oven to 200 °C.\n- Pass your 500 g of cooked russet potatoes through a potato ricer into a large bowl.\n- Stir in 2 large egg yolks and 118 mL of whole milk.\n- Mix in the first 250 g bag of shredded cheese.\n- Add the potato seasoning base: 19.5 mL salt, 29.5 mL black pepper, 15 mL dill, 29.5 mL garlic powder, 15 mL oregano, 15 mL rosemary, 5 mL lemon pepper, and 10 mL beef bouillon powder. Stir well and set aside",
    "html": "<ul>\n<li>Preheat your oven to <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"200 °C\" data-original=\"200°C (400°F)\" data-us=\"400 °F\" title=\"Source: 200°C (400°F). The original recipe provides this rounded Celsius/Fahrenheit pair.\">200 °C</span>.</li>\n<li>Pass your <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"500 g\" data-original=\"500g\" data-us=\"17.64 oz\" title=\"Source: 500g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">500 g</span> of cooked russet potatoes through a potato ricer into a large bowl.</li>\n<li>Stir in 2 large egg yolks and <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"118 mL\" data-original=\"1/2 cup\" data-us=\"½ cup\" title=\"Source: 1/2 cup. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">118 mL</span> of whole milk.</li>\n<li>Mix in the first <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"250 g\" data-original=\"250g\" data-us=\"8.82 oz\" title=\"Source: 250g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">250 g</span> bag of shredded cheese.</li>\n<li>Add the potato seasoning base: <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"19.5 mL\" data-original=\"4 tsps\" data-us=\"4 tsp\" title=\"Source: 4 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">19.5 mL</span> salt, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> black pepper, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 mL\" data-original=\"1 tbsp\" data-us=\"1 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tbsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">15 mL</span> dill, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> garlic powder, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 mL\" data-original=\"1 tbsp\" data-us=\"1 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tbsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">15 mL</span> oregano, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"15 mL\" data-original=\"1 tbsp\" data-us=\"1 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tbsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">15 mL</span> rosemary, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"5 mL\" data-original=\"1 tsp\" data-us=\"1 tsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">5 mL</span> lemon pepper, and <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> beef bouillon powder. Stir well and set aside </li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-4",
    "title": "Step 1: Mash and Season the Potatoes",
    "heading_html": "Step 1: Mash and Season the Potatoes"
  },
  "recipe-section-5": {
    "markdown": "- Set your Instant Pot to its sauté function and add 29.5 mL of olive oil.\n- Drop in 1 kg of ground beef (it is perfectly fine if it is still halfway frozen). Begin breaking it apart.\n- Pulse your onion in a food processor and press 9 cloves of garlic. Toss them directly into the pot with the browning beef.\n- Pour in a 100 mL splash of vodka to help build depth of flavor",
    "html": "<ul>\n<li>Set your Instant Pot to its sauté function and add <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> of olive oil.</li>\n<li>Drop in <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"1 kg\" data-original=\"1000g\" data-us=\"2.2 lb\" title=\"Source: 1000g. 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces.\">1 kg</span> of ground beef (it is perfectly fine if it is still halfway frozen). Begin breaking it apart.</li>\n<li>Pulse your onion in a food processor and press 9 cloves of garlic. Toss them directly into the pot with the browning beef.</li>\n<li>Pour in a <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"100 mL\" data-original=\"100ml\" data-us=\"0.42 cup\" title=\"Source: 100ml. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">100 mL</span> splash of vodka to help build depth of flavor</li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-5",
    "title": "Step 2: Brown the Meat with Aromatics",
    "heading_html": "Step 2: Brown the Meat with Aromatics"
  },
  "recipe-section-6": {
    "markdown": "- While the beef continues cooking down, add the meat seasonings: 29.5 mL chicken bouillon, 29.5 mL lemon pepper, 29.5 mL Tajín, 5 mL ginger powder, 29.5 mL garlic powder, 10 mL rosemary, 10 mL oregano, 10 mL dill, and 5 mL salt.\n- Pour in 237 mL of water and stir to dissolve the bouillon powder.\n- Add 59 mL of tomato paste to change the liquid baseline.\n- Dust 30 g of all-purpose flour over the mixture. Stir it consistently for a few minutes until the sauce reduces into a thick, chunky chili-like consistency. *Note: It is fine if some meat pieces remain slightly pink before baking*",
    "html": "<ul>\n<li>While the beef continues cooking down, add the meat seasonings: <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> chicken bouillon, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> lemon pepper, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> Tajín, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"5 mL\" data-original=\"1 tsp\" data-us=\"1 tsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">5 mL</span> ginger powder, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"29.5 mL\" data-original=\"2 tbsps\" data-us=\"2 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">29.5 mL</span> garlic powder, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> rosemary, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> oregano, <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"10 mL\" data-original=\"2 tsps\" data-us=\"2 tsp\" title=\"Source: 2 tsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">10 mL</span> dill, and <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"5 mL\" data-original=\"1 tsp\" data-us=\"1 tsp\" title=\"Source: 1 tsp. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">5 mL</span> salt.</li>\n<li>Pour in <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"237 mL\" data-original=\"1 cup\" data-us=\"1 cup\" title=\"Source: 1 cup. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">237 mL</span> of water and stir to dissolve the bouillon powder.</li>\n<li>Add <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"59 mL\" data-original=\"4 tbsps\" data-us=\"4 tbsp\" title=\"Source: 4 tbsps. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">59 mL</span> of tomato paste to change the liquid baseline.</li>\n<li>Dust <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"30 g\" data-original=\"30g (2 tbsps)\" data-us=\"1.06 oz\" title=\"Source: 30g (2 tbsps). 1 oz = 28.349523125 g; 1 lb = 453.59237 g; ounces are weight, not fluid ounces. Explicit metric quantity retained instead of the source's approximate equivalent.\">30 g</span> of all-purpose flour over the mixture. Stir it consistently for a few minutes until the sauce reduces into a thick, chunky chili-like consistency. <em>Note: It is fine if some meat pieces remain slightly pink before baking</em></li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-6",
    "title": "Step 3: Spice and Thicken the Gravy",
    "heading_html": "Step 3: Spice and Thicken the Gravy"
  },
  "recipe-section-7": {
    "markdown": "- Turn off the Instant Pot heat. Stir in 237 mL of frozen mixed vegetables and let them sit in the hot meat mixture for 2 minutes to thaw.\n- Transfer the entire thick beef mix into the bottom of a 9x13 baking dish.\n- Sprinkle a light coating of cheese from your second bag directly over the hot meat layer",
    "html": "<ul>\n<li>Turn off the Instant Pot heat. Stir in <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"237 mL\" data-original=\"1 cup\" data-us=\"1 cup\" title=\"Source: 1 cup. 1 US cup = 236.5882365 mL; 1 tbsp = 1/16 cup; 1 tsp = 1/48 cup. Volume is not treated as mass.\">237 mL</span> of frozen mixed vegetables and let them sit in the hot meat mixture for 2 minutes to thaw.</li>\n<li>Transfer the entire thick beef mix into the bottom of a 9x13 baking dish.</li>\n<li>Sprinkle a light coating of cheese from your second bag directly over the hot meat layer</li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-7",
    "title": "Step 4: Incorporate Vegetables and Assemble",
    "heading_html": "Step 4: Incorporate Vegetables and Assemble"
  },
  "recipe-section-8": {
    "markdown": "- Spread your seasoned mashed potatoes evenly across the top of the cheese and beef layer.\n- Empty the remaining shredded cheese from the second bag across the entire top surface of the potatoes to ensure a gorgeous crust forms.\n- Bake uncovered at 200 °C for exactly 20 minutes until the top cheese is bubbly and golden brown.\n- Garnish with an extra pinch of dill right out of the oven and serve hot",
    "html": "<ul>\n<li>Spread your seasoned mashed potatoes evenly across the top of the cheese and beef layer.</li>\n<li>Empty the remaining shredded cheese from the second bag across the entire top surface of the potatoes to ensure a gorgeous crust forms.</li>\n<li>Bake uncovered at <span class=\"measure\" data-metric=\"200 °C\" data-original=\"200°C (400°F)\" data-us=\"400 °F\" title=\"Source: 200°C (400°F). The original recipe provides this rounded Celsius/Fahrenheit pair.\">200 °C</span> for exactly 20 minutes until the top cheese is bubbly and golden brown.</li>\n<li>Garnish with an extra pinch of dill right out of the oven and serve hot</li>\n</ul>",
    "id": "recipe-section-8",
    "title": "Step 5: Top and Bake",
    "heading_html": "Step 5: Top and Bake"
  }
}
